 a player component that you can control and how to add text and various labels to your game scene."}],"kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/CreateFirst2DScene#Make-it-move":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial, you will learn how to create your first 2D scene using Ada."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Make-it-move","title":"Make it move","role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/createfirst2dscene#Make-it-move","type":"section"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/UIBasics#Create-the-app-shell":{"url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/uibasics#Create-the-app-shell","type":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics#Create-the-app-shell","title":"Create the app shell","abstract":[{"text":"Build a simple UI screen using Ada views. You will create a window, layout a few elements, and add a button with state.","type":"text"}],"kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/GamepadInput":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a small scene that spawns a player entity and moves it with a gamepad."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput","title":"Gamepad Input","role":"project","kind":"project","url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/gamepadinput","estimatedTime":"20min","type":"topic"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/GamepadInput#Create-the-input-system":{"url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/gamepadinput#Create-the-input-system","type":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput#Create-the-input-system","title":"Create the input system","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a small scene that spawns a player entity and moves it with a gamepad."}],"kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/CreateProject#Create-project-using-Xcode":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateProject#Create-project-using-Xcode","abstract":[{"text":"In this tutorial, you will learn how to create your first Ada project.","type":"text"}],"title":"Create project using Xcode","role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/createproject#Create-project-using-Xcode","type":"section"},"EL-2-4-events.swift":{"type":"file","highlights":[],"identifier":"EL-2-4-events.swift","fileName":"Events.swift","content":["\/\/\/ Events the scene triggers.","public enum SceneEvents {","","    \/\/\/ An event triggered once when scene is ready to use and will starts update soon.","    public struct OnReady: Event {","        public let scene: Scene","    }","","    \/\/\/ Raised after an entity is added to the scene.","    public struct DidAddEntity: Event {","        public let entity: Entity","    }","","    \/\/\/ Raised before an entity is removed from the scene.","    public struct WillRemoveEntity: Event {","        public let entity: Entity","    }","","    \/\/\/ An event triggered once per frame interval that you can use to execute custom logic for each frame.","    public struct Update: Event {","","        \/\/\/ The updated scene.","        public let scene: Scene","","        \/\/\/ The elapsed time since the last update.","        public let deltaTime: TimeInterval","    }","}","","\/\/\/ Events associated with collisions.","public enum CollisionEvents {","","    \/\/\/ An event raised when two objects collide.","    public struct Began: Event {","","        \/\/\/ The first entity involved in the collision.","        public let entityA: Entity","","        \/\/\/ The second entity involved in the collision.","        public let entityB: Entity","","        \/\/\/ The estimated strength of the impact.","        public let impulse: Float","    }","","    \/\/\/ An event raised when two objects, previously in contact, separate.","    public struct Ended: Event {","","        \/\/\/ The first entity involved in the collision.","        public let entityA: Entity","","        \/\/\/ The second entity involved in the collision.","        public let entityB: Entity","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","fileType":"swift"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/AnimatedText#Apply-and-animate":{"url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/animatedtext#Apply-and-animate","type":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/AnimatedText#Apply-and-animate","title":"Apply and animate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a custom "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TextRenderer"},{"type":"text","text":" that draws text along a sine wave and animate it by updating renderer state."}],"kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/UIBasics":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a simple UI screen using Ada views. You will create a window, layout a few elements, and add a button with state."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics","title":"UI Basics","role":"project","kind":"project","url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/uibasics","estimatedTime":"15min","type":"topic"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/CreateFirst2DScene#Create-an-app":{"url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/createfirst2dscene#Create-an-app","type":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Create-an-app","title":"Create an app","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial, you will learn how to create your first 2D scene using Ada."}],"kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/CreateFirst2DScene#Intro":{"url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/createfirst2dscene#Intro","type":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Intro","title":"Intro","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial, you will learn how to create your first 2D scene using Ada."}],"kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/CreateProject":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial, you will